THOUGHT: The error is that applicationContext is marked @Nullable but passed to a constructor expecting @NonNull. Since Factory implements ApplicationContextAware, create() should only be called after the context is set. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll add a defensive null check that throws an IllegalStateException if applicationContext is still null, ensuring only a non-null value is passed to the constructor. Then I’ll run the compile task to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '237,239c\			ConfigurationPropertiesBinder create() {
			ApplicationContext applicationContext = this.applicationContext;
			if (applicationContext == null) {
				throw new IllegalStateException("ApplicationContext has not been set");
			}
			return new ConfigurationPropertiesBinder(applicationContext);
		}' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/context/properties/ConfigurationPropertiesBinder.java && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

